{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underprediction: when the last 5–10 days show a sustained rally (higher highs / higher lows), the model level is systematically too low across the whole horizon. Apply an additive uplift that grows with horizon (small in days 1–3, larger by days 10–30).",
    "Trend/acceleration lag: the model reacts too slowly to regime shifts (Dec rally). Use a momentum term based on recent slope (e.g., 5–10d linear trend) and add it forward; effectively shift the forecast path upward in strong momentum periods.",
    "Horizon-specific bias: errors increase with lead time. Calibrate a lead-dependent correction (e.g., +X for days 1–5, +2X for days 6–15, +3X for days 16–30) during trending markets.",
    "Post-spike behavior: after a sharp jump, the model tends to mean-revert too early/too much (forecasts flatten/fall while realized stays elevated). Reduce mean-reversion strength for ~1–2 weeks after a breakout; keep forecasts closer to the new level.",
    "Late-sample reversal risk: in early Jan the realized series peaks then declines; the model still underpredicts but begins to capture the downturn earlier than realized in some paths. After an extended rally (e.g., >+10 over 2–3 weeks), temper the uplift beyond ~day 20 and allow mild downward drift."
  ]
}
